# Frontend Architecture Guide

## Application Structure

### Core Directories
- [src/app/](mdc:src/app) - Next.js 13+ app router pages and layouts
- [src/components/](mdc:src/components) - Reusable React components
- [src/contexts/](mdc:src/contexts) - React context providers
- [src/hooks/](mdc:src/hooks) - Custom React hooks
- [src/websocket-server/](mdc:src/websocket-server) - Real-time communication server

## Component Organization

### UI Components
- Atomic design principles
- Component-specific styling with Tailwind CSS
- TypeScript interfaces for props
- JSDoc documentation for complex components

### State Management
- React Context for global state
- Custom hooks for shared logic
- WebSocket integration for real-time updates

## Real-time Communication

### WebSocket Server
- Handles device connections
- Manages real-time state updates
- Implements reconnection logic
- Provides event system for components

### Data Flow
1. Device state changes
2. WebSocket server processes update
3. Frontend components receive updates
4. UI reflects new state

